1. e4 c6 2. Nf3 d5 3. Nc3 { The Two Knights Variation The Two Knights Variation is a positional and
solid opening against the Caro Kann. White develops two pieces ahead of
black and is looking forward to an easy play. Since white has developed two pieces ahead of black, black should catch up in development right away.
Black has to take the pawn so white's knight would be forced to waste a tempo followed by Nbd7 to Nf6. Following the Caro Kann Karpov Variation. } 3... dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nd7 5. d4 Ngf6 6. Ng3 { Eventually, we are back to the Classical Caro Kann. } 6... e6 7. Bd3 Be7 8. O-O O-O 9. Bf4 b6 10. Re1 Bb7 11. Qe2 c5 { Caro Kann: https://lichess.org/study/ZziYzSGs } *


