1. e4 c6 2. Nf3 d5 3. Nc3 { The Two Knights Variation The Two Knights Variation is a positional and
solid opening against the Caro Kann. White develops two pieces ahead of
black and is looking forward to an easy play. Since white has developed two pieces ahead of black, black should catch up in development right away.
Black has to take the pawn so white's knight would be forced to waste a tempo followed by Nbd7 to Nf6. Following the Caro Kann Karpov Variation. } 3... dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nd7 5. Qe2 { White is aiming for the opening trap of Nd6 checkmate. Either ways this
isn't white's one any only plan. White also wants to dominate the e file
once white castles kingside or queenside followed by either rook to e1. White is going to develop is pieces with ease. Black should also do the same,
just beware of checkmating ideas. } 5... e6 6. d4 Ngf6 7. Nxf6+ Nxf6 8. Bf4 Bd6 9. Bxd6 Qxd6 10. O-O-O O-O 11. h4 { As soon as white eventually launches a pawn storm around the kingside.
Black should also aim to attack white's queenside aswell by launching a
pawn storm on the queenside. Its only a matter of time before both opposing sides defend against the potential threat of checkmates. } 11... b5 12. h5 h6 13. Qe5 Qd5 *


