1. e4 c6 2. c4 { This is the Panov Attack The Panov Attack is an aggressive opening choice
against the Caro Kann. First of all white voluntarily creates an isolated
pawn which would be a clear target for black to take on. Second of all White is willing to create weaknesses in exchange for initiative and attack.
Even a pawn sacrifice would not matter if white has enough counterplay. Black's goal is to further fortify the position. Develop the pieces with ease and is looking forward to a great game. } 2... d5 3. Nc3 { White may even play Nc3 to experiment and put black out of his comfort
zone. } 3... d4 4. Nce2 e5 5. d3 Nd7 6. f4 Bb4+ 7. Bd2 Bxd2+ 8. Qxd2 f6 9. Nf3 Nh6 10. Ng3 { Position is frankly doing alright for black in here. } 10... O-O *


