1. e4 c6 2. d3 { d3 is a positional way of handling the Caro Kann, eventually white is not
looking for a quick or aggressive attack but rather would play a positional
and quiet game. This however may not be the strongest option for white but it is a quiet and positional response when it comes to defensive play. } (2. g3) 2... d5 3. Nd2 { [%anno "ShreksGonGiveItToYa", shreksgongiveittoya] Eventually white is aiming for a King's Indian Structure in here. Ngf3 g3
Bg2 0-0 Is white's idea in here. } 3... e5 { Black should be aware of the fact that white is voluntarily giving black
the opportunity to take over the center. Black should grab that
opportunity! } 4. Ngf3 Bd6 5. g3 { Other alternative includes the move d4! But eventually the move g3 is by
far more safer for white. Bg2 followed by short castle is frankly alright
for white in here. } 5... Bg4 6. Bg2 Nf6 7. h3 Bxf3 8. Nxf3 O-O { Caro Kann: https://lichess.org/study/ZziYzSGs } *


